@lang en

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-application`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-schedule1`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-definitions`

-- Tests for uk-interpretation-definitions.l4: the structured entries of Schedule 1 and Schedule 2 paras 4(2), 4(3), 4(5), 4(6) and 5.
--
-- Each expected value below was decided by reading the entry or paragraph, and written down before the module was run. An entry that "includes" is tried with a
-- thing it names, a thing it does not name, and the exceptions it states. A failing assertion is a finding.
-- The days and numbers that the Act borrows from other texts (the day the Irish Free State was established, the day the Welsh Language Act 1967 was passed, the day
-- the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1975 came into force, the limit that the Sentencing Code lays down) are INPUTS; the values used here are illustrations
-- and are not claims about those texts.

§ `Schedule 1 "British Islands" and Schedule 2 para 4(2)`

-- "means the United Kingdom, the Channel Islands and the Isle of Man". The Irish Free State is taken to have been established on 6 December 1922 (an input).
#ASSERT `Schedule 1 counts the place as part of the British Islands for an Act passed on` `the United Kingdom` (YMD 1950 1 1) (YMD 1922 12 6)
#ASSERT `Schedule 1 counts the place as part of the British Islands for an Act passed on` `the Channel Islands` (YMD 1950 1 1) (YMD 1922 12 6)
#ASSERT `Schedule 1 counts the place as part of the British Islands for an Act passed on` `the Isle of Man` (YMD 1950 1 1) (YMD 1922 12 6)
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 1 counts the place as part of the British Islands for an Act passed on` `another place` (YMD 1950 1 1) (YMD 1922 12 6)
-- Para 4(2): for an Act passed after the establishment and before the commencement, the Republic of Ireland is included.
#ASSERT `Schedule 1 counts the place as part of the British Islands for an Act passed on` `the Republic of Ireland` (YMD 1922 12 7) (YMD 1922 12 6)
#ASSERT `Schedule 1 counts the place as part of the British Islands for an Act passed on` `the Republic of Ireland` (YMD 1978 12 31) (YMD 1922 12 6)
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 1 counts the place as part of the British Islands for an Act passed on` `the Republic of Ireland` (YMD 1922 12 5) (YMD 1922 12 6)
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 1 counts the place as part of the British Islands for an Act passed on` `the Republic of Ireland` (YMD 1979 1 1) (YMD 1922 12 6)
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 1 counts the place as part of the British Islands for an Act passed on` `the Republic of Ireland` (YMD 2026 3 10) (YMD 1922 12 6)
-- An Act passed on the very day: the paragraph does not say (fork F22).
#ASSERT REFUSED `Schedule 1 counts the place as part of the British Islands for an Act passed on` `the Republic of Ireland` (YMD 1922 12 6) (YMD 1922 12 6) BECAUSE "Schedule 2 para 4(2) does not say whether an Act passed on the day the Irish Free State was established was passed after it"

§ `Schedule 1 "British possession", "Colonial legislature", "Colony" and "Governor-General"`

#ASSERT `Schedule 1 counts the territory as a British possession` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 1 counts the territory as a British possession` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 1 counts the territory as a British possession` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 1 counts the territory as a British possession` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Schedule 1 treats the parts under a central legislature as one British possession` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 1 treats the parts under a central legislature as one British possession` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 1 treats the parts under a central legislature as one British possession` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 1 treats the parts under a central legislature as one British possession` FALSE FALSE

-- "the authority, other than the Parliament of the United Kingdom or Her Majesty in Council, competent to make laws for the possession"
#ASSERT `Schedule 1 counts the authority as a colonial legislature` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 1 counts the authority as a colonial legislature` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 1 counts the authority as a colonial legislature` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 1 counts the authority as a colonial legislature` FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- "any part of Her Majesty's dominions outside the British Islands except (a) ..., (b) ..., (c) ..."
#ASSERT `Schedule 1 counts the territory as a colony` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 1 counts the territory as a colony` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 1 counts the territory as a colony` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 1 counts the territory as a colony` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 1 counts the territory as a colony` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Schedule 1 treats the parts under a central legislature as one colony` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 1 treats the parts under a central legislature as one colony` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 1 treats the parts under a central legislature as one colony` FALSE TRUE

-- "Governor-General includes any person who for the time being has the powers of the Governor-General, and Governor, in relation to any British possession, includes the officer for the time being administering the government of that possession"
#ASSERT `Schedule 1 counts the person as a Governor-General or Governor` `Governor-General` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 1 counts the person as a Governor-General or Governor` `Governor-General` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Schedule 1 counts the person as a Governor-General or Governor` `Governor, in relation to a British possession` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 1 counts the person as a Governor-General or Governor` `Governor, in relation to a British possession` TRUE FALSE

§ `Schedule 2 para 4(3): "colony" for an Act passed before the commencement`

-- Paragraph (b) of the definition does not apply to an Act passed before the commencement: a territory for whose external relations another country is responsible IS a colony for it.
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 para 4(3) counts the territory as a colony for an Act passed on` (YMD 1978 12 31) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 2 para 4(3) counts the territory as a colony for an Act passed on` (YMD 1979 1 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING FALSE
-- Paragraphs (a) and (c) of the definition still apply to it.
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 2 para 4(3) counts the territory as a colony for an Act passed on` (YMD 1950 1 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 2 para 4(3) counts the territory as a colony for an Act passed on` (YMD 1950 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING FALSE
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 para 4(3) counts the territory as a colony for an Act passed on` (YMD 1950 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 2 para 4(3) counts the territory as a colony for an Act passed on` (YMD 1950 1 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING FALSE
-- (a): a colony within section 18(3) of the 1889 Act that an enactment repealed by this Act excluded, but only for Acts passed at a later time.
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 para 4(3) counts the territory as a colony for an Act passed on` (YMD 1949 12 31) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (JUST (YMD 1950 1 1)) NOTHING FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 2 para 4(3) counts the territory as a colony for an Act passed on` (YMD 1950 1 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (JUST (YMD 1950 1 1)) NOTHING FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 2 para 4(3) counts the territory as a colony for an Act passed on` (YMD 1949 12 31) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST (YMD 1950 1 1)) NOTHING FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 2 para 4(3) counts the territory as a colony for an Act passed on` (YMD 1949 12 31) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE NOTHING NOTHING FALSE
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 para 4(3)(a) provides that the Act was passed before the exclusion took effect` (YMD 1949 12 31) (JUST (YMD 1950 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 2 para 4(3)(a) provides that the Act was passed before the exclusion took effect` (YMD 1950 1 1) (JUST (YMD 1950 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 2 para 4(3)(a) provides that the Act was passed before the exclusion took effect` (YMD 1949 12 31) NOTHING
-- (b): a country or territory that ceased after that time to be part of Her Majesty's dominions, subject to a provision continuing the existing law.
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 para 4(3) counts the territory as a colony for an Act passed on` (YMD 1959 12 31) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING (JUST (YMD 1960 1 1)) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 2 para 4(3) counts the territory as a colony for an Act passed on` (YMD 1960 1 2) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING (JUST (YMD 1960 1 1)) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 2 para 4(3) counts the territory as a colony for an Act passed on` (YMD 1959 12 31) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING (JUST (YMD 1960 1 1)) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 2 para 4(3) counts the territory as a colony for an Act passed on` (YMD 1959 12 31) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING TRUE
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 para 4(3)(b) provides that the territory ceased after the Act was passed to be part of Her Majesty's dominions` (YMD 1959 12 31) (JUST (YMD 1960 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 2 para 4(3)(b) provides that the territory ceased after the Act was passed to be part of Her Majesty's dominions` (YMD 1960 1 2) (JUST (YMD 1960 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 2 para 4(3)(b) provides that the territory ceased after the Act was passed to be part of Her Majesty's dominions` (YMD 1959 12 31) NOTHING
#ASSERT REFUSED `Schedule 2 para 4(3)(b) provides that the territory ceased after the Act was passed to be part of Her Majesty's dominions` (YMD 1960 1 1) (JUST (YMD 1960 1 1)) BECAUSE "Schedule 2 para 4(3)(b) does not say whether a territory that ceased on the day the Act was passed ceased after it"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Schedule 2 para 4(3) counts the territory as a colony for an Act passed on` (YMD 1960 1 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING (JUST (YMD 1960 1 1)) TRUE BECAUSE "Schedule 2 para 4(3)(b) does not say whether a territory that ceased on the day the Act was passed ceased after it"

