§ `Schedule 2 para 5(a) and (c)`

-- (a) in any Act passed before 1st April 1974, a reference to England includes Berwick upon Tweed and Monmouthshire and, in the case of an Act passed before the
-- Welsh Language Act 1967, Wales. The day of that Act is an input (27 July 1967 is an illustration).
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 para 5(a) provides that a reference to England includes the place in an Act passed on` `Berwick upon Tweed` (YMD 1974 3 31) (YMD 1967 7 27)
